192] ListItem: Wake \u2014 Say \"Pulse.\" It responds: \"I'm listening.\" @top-center", "[193] ListItem: Understand \u2014 Pulse interprets your intent rather than requiring exact commands:  @top-center", "[194] ListItem: Plan \u2014 Pulse breaks the request into a sequence of safe, concrete actions. @top-center", "[195] ListItem: Execute \u2014 Pulse performs each step, narrating progress as it goes. @top-center", "[196] ListItem: Confirm \u2014 Sensitive actions (deleting files, closing unsaved work) always ask fi @top-center", "[197] Hyperlink: Architecture @top-left", "[198] Hyperlink: Permalink: Features @top-left", "[199] Hyperlink: Permalink: Core Principles @top-left", "[200] ListItem: Accessibility First \u2014 every interaction reduces uncertainty by keeping the user  @top-center", "[201] ListItem: Voice First \u2014 voice is the primary interface; no keyboard shortcuts required. @top-center", "[202] ListItem: Local & Private \u2014 planning, speech recognition, and text-to-speech all run on-de @top-center", "[203] ListItem: Human Control \u2014 Pulse never silently performs a sensitive action; you stay in co @top-center", "[204] Hyperlink: Permalink: What Pulse Can Do Today @top-left", "[205] ListItem: Open and close applications, files, and folders by name or description @top-center", "[206] ListItem: Read what's actually on screen (buttons, fields, links, visible text) to decide  @top-center", "[207] ListItem: Fall back to real visual analysis of a screenshot when text alone is ambiguous ( @top-center", "[208] ListItem: Click, fill in fields, and send keyboard shortcuts across arbitrary Windows apps @top-center", "[209] ListItem: Drive the standard Windows Save dialog end-to-end (type a path, confirm, verify  @top-center", "[210] ListItem: Search the local filesystem and the web @top-center", "[211] ListItem: Understand natural-language requests and hold a short back-and-forth to fill in  @top-center", "[212] ListItem: Break a request into multiple step