to start fresh, then restart Pulse and execute the test.", "All four changes verified individually. Now restarting Pulse and re-running the live Word test with the same logging discipline as before.", "I should clean up any leftover test files from previous attempts\u2014specifically checking if pulse_word_test.docx exists on the Desktop or OneDrive and removing it so the test starts fresh without any stale files interfering with the save logic.", "No existing file to worry about, so I can start fresh. Time to launch Pulse through run.bat.", "I need to check the end of the log file to see if there's a more recent \"Pulse is running\" message beyond the 00:43:37 timestamp, and verify whether the PreferCloudSaveLocations setting is still being logged.", "I'm trying to figure out which restart I'm actually looking at\u2014the timestamp from 00:43:37 could be from my earlier manual test of the office_prefs module, but that wouldn't have produced the \"Pulse is running\" log line since it was just a standalone script. So I must have actually restarted pulse.p", "The Pulse instance restarted cleanly at 00:43:20 AM, which matches the log confirmation, so I'm working with a fresh baseline of 1051 lines. Now I'll run the Word test command to see what happens.", "Confirmed fresh instance running. Sending the Word test now.", "Watching now \u2014 will report as events come in.", "I'm noticing that the SEND response immediately used the \"OVERALL GOAL:\" prefix, which suggests the first response already contained a valid task_list\u2014either the initial attempt succeeded with multiple tasks, or my corrective retry worked. Let me review the full first response to confirm whether tas", "The validation and retry mechanism caught the exact same issue again\u2014the model's reasoning said it would use the task_list format, but the JSON output was missing that field entirely. My detection logic triggered the corrective retry, and the second attempt succeeded within seconds.\n\nNow I'm examini", "The", "task_list", "fix just worked in real time \u2014 first response omitted it despite saying it should, my corrective retry fired, and the second response properly included it. Now running through", "_execute_task_list", "'s per-step isolation as intended. Continuing to watch.", "The Word window failure is actually an environmental issue\u2014since I'm running this remotely through SSH and automation tools rather than an interactive desktop session, the workstation might have a locked screen or no active foreground window, which explains the \"no focusable windows\" error. Let me i", "So `LogonUI.exe` is actually running, which confirms the workstation is genuinely locked right now\u2014this matches the documented behavior where `GetForegroundWindow()` legitimately returns 0 during a lock. This is an environmental issue from the screen timing out during the test, not a bug in the code", "The workstation's screen has locked (inactivity timeout) \u2014", "LogonUI.exe", "is running, confirming it. The model actually handled this correctly, reporting it as a real blocker instead of looping, but the live test can't proceed further until the screen is unlocked.", "Could you unlock the screen when you get a chance so I can re-run the Word test? Everything else is staged and ready \u2014 I'll pick the test back up as soon as it's unlocked.", "5 minutes ago", "You said: screen unlocked try again", "screen unlocked try again", "I need to verify the screen is unlocked before resending the test, and I should clear out any previous state first.", "The screen is unlocked since the LogonUI process isn't running, so I'll clean up the failed test rows from the database and resend the test fresh while the app is still running.", "Confirmed unlocked. Cleaning up the previous locked-screen attempt and resending.", "I should close any Word windows that might have opened during the locked-screen attempt, establish a baseline for the pulse.log line count, and then resend