 while the app is still running.", "Confirmed unlocked. Cleaning up the previous locked-screen attempt and resending.", "I should close any Word windows that might have opened during the locked-screen attempt, establish a baseline for the pulse.log line count, and then resend to get a clean state.", "Watching now.", "The task_list inclusion in the first response is working as expected, so the fix is holding up well.", "task_list", "came through correctly on the first try this time \u2014 no retry needed. Continuing to watch.", "I'm noticing something odd here\u2014the history from the previous locked-screen attempt shouldn't be bleeding into this fresh task since I created a new task_id, but I'm wondering if \"history\" is referring to something else entirely, like the conversation manager's internal state rather than the actual ", "I'm noticing that Step 1 is being reprocessed even though we already completed an app open earlier, which suggests the workflow might be stuck on the first step rather than progressing to the next one. Let me examine the full context to determine whether this is a legitimate re-confirmation or an ac", "I'm noticing this is the same stale context issue I identified before\u2014the system prompt has \"the current screen context is Claude\" locked in from the start and never gets refreshed. The step framing keeps saying \"Step 1 of 3: Open Word\" even as it's analyzing its own position within that step's exec", "I'm noticing that the response included a task list with three items nested inside the output structure, which means the nested_task_list in the round-processing logic has a length of 3. I need to figure out what iteration we're at \u2014 since this is happening within Step 2's observation call and we're", "Good \u2014 this time a spurious", "task_list", "appeared mid-step again, but the", "iteration == 0", "gate correctly caught it and did NOT restart the whole task \u2014 it just triggered one redundant (harmless)", "open_app", "c